  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_011: image_only, singleprofile, resnet50 → acc 0.208, F1 0.172), which is barely above chance, indicating the task is difficult or the current representation is insufficient. The most critical uncertainty right now is whether the low performance is due to a weak image encoder or a fundamental ceiling of the image modality. Config_039 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_011—only the image encoder changes from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L, holding profile setting, aggregation, and fusion constant. If ViT-L substantially outperforms ResNet50, we learn that representation quality is the bottleneck and should prioritize stronger encoders in multimodal settings. If it does not, we gain strong evidence that the image modality alone has a low ceiling and that RNA information (or multiprofile aggregation) is the more important axis to explore next. This experiment maximizes information gain per budget unit by isolating one key design variable without introducing confounds from modality, profile, or fusion changes."
}

